# CI after push (blocking)

**A push is not done until required workflows are green** on that branch. Do not end the
session, open a PR as ready, or mark work complete after `git push` without watching.

## Workflows (monorepo)

| Branch | Workflow | Must pass |
|--------|----------|-----------|
| Any | `.github/workflows/ci-cd.yml` | Test matrix (+ alembic/native as required) |
| `stage` | same | **Deploy (stage)** + **Staging smoke** (after merge/push) |
| `main` | same | **Deploy (main)** to prod; PRs need **Staging gate** |

Workflows live at **monorepo root** (`../` from this backend package when checked out alone).

## After every push (required)

```bash
# From monorepo root
gh run list --branch "$(git branch --show-current)" --workflow ci-cd.yml --limit 3
gh run watch <run-id>
```

| Outcome | Action |
|---------|--------|
| **success** | Record run URL; proceed |
| **failure** | `gh run view <run-id> --log-failed` → fix → push → re-watch |
| **User waives** | AskQuestion only; note waiver in PR/summary |

## Before the first push (local parity — monorepo root)

```bash
make format-check    # ruff format --check apps packages tests + pnpm format:check
make lint
make typecheck
make test-unit       # or make ci for full pre-commit parity
```

Quality Gates scope is **`apps packages tests`** — not legacy `src/` paths. Bug repro tests
under `tests/bugs/` are both format/lint-checked **and executed**: they run as the `bugs`
matrix entry of the `ci-cd.yml` `test` job and via `make test-bugs` (included in
`make test-unit` / `make ci`). See `ci-quality-gates.mdc`.

